  "configuration_id": "config_021",
  "reason": "Evidence: The three completed experiments show a clear trend—scvi_n200 RNA encoder outperforms pca_n2000 (0.678 vs 0.639 with resnet50), and imagenet_vit_l outperforms resnet50 (0.706 vs 0.678 with scvi_n200). The current best (config_045, 0.706) uses avgpool aggregation and weighted fusion. Question: Can transformer aggregation, which learns attention-weighted interactions across profiles, improve over simple average pooling in the multiprofile setting? Config_021 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) isolates the aggregation change while keeping the best-validated encoders and fusion. This is the most impactful untested architectural lever: avgpool treats all profiles symmetrically, while a transformer can adaptively weight profiles based on content, potentially capturing complementary signals. Rationale: With 6 experiments remaining, exploiting the strongest encoder combination while testing the highest-impact remaining design choice (aggregation) is the best use of the next slot. Expected relative cost: moderately higher than config_045 (4.82 GPU hrs) due to self-attention over profiles on ViT-L features; estimated ~7–9 GPU hrs, roughly 1.5–1.8× the current best."
}

